From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Winter <danielwinterw@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:37:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] models: add Qwen3-MoE native MTP

Load an appended NextN block for qwen3moe and build its draft graph, so a
Qwen3-MoE checkpoint with a trained multi-token-prediction head drafts
through the existing native MTP sidecar path, unsplit and on the final
stage of a split.

The head is one dense Qwen3 decoder layer (attention shaped like the
trunk's, SwiGLU FFN sized by its own tensors) fed by
eh_proj([enorm(e_{t+1}); hnorm(h_t)]), where h_t is the trunk's post-norm
hidden state. Logits come from the shared LM head after shared_head_norm;
deeper drafts chain on the layer output before that norm, which is what
the MTP graph exposes as its NextN hidden state.

The trunk keeps every row's post-norm hidden state when NextN outputs are
unmasked. The converter appends a head stored beside the checkpoint as
mtp.safetensors + mtp_config.json, swapping proj's input halves into the
GGUF eh_proj concat order, and --mtp exports it as a draft sidecar. A
synthetic fixture certifies the integrated stage program and its drafts.
